Multiple data declines see poor Taiwan economy starts the year unfavorably - CNET China
Xinhua Taipei, February 11 (Xinhua reporters Zhao Bo and Huang Yang) Exports fell for five consecutive months, the manufacturing purchasing managers' index (PMI) contracted for seven consecutive months, and the consumer price index (CPI) hit "three-digit" again... In recent days, Taiwan's authorities have successively released economic data for January 2023.
Experts believe that Taiwan’s economic performance in the new year has been disappointing and growth pressures are mounting.
According to Taiwan’s authorities’ financial affairs department, Taiwan region’s exports reached $31.51 billion in January, down 21.2% year-on-year and for the fifth consecutive month of negative growth.
The export value of the 11 major export categories has declined compared to the same period last year.
Rubber and plastics, as well as their products, and optical equipment saw the steepest declines, with year-over-year reductions of 37.6% and 35.7%, respectively.
Electronic component exports fell 20.1% year-on-year, marking the largest decline in 11 years.
Among them, integrated circuits declined 18.3% year-on-year, marking the largest drop in 14 years.
Department of Statistics Director Cai Minna said this indicates that the weakness in consumer electronics industry demand is spreading, and the electronic industry is entering a correction phase.
Statistics show that Taiwan's imports and exports both declined in January, with a trade surplus of just $2.34 billion, the lowest level in nearly three years.
The Taiwan authorities’ finance bureau believes that global terminal demand is declining, industrial adjustments in inventory will suppress manufacturers' purchasing intentions for materials, and export weakness may not improve temporarily. The Taiwanese first-quarter exports could be worse than expected this year.
According to the Central Institute of Economic Management in Taiwan, the seasonally adjusted Purchasing Managers' Index (PMI) for Taiwan's manufacturing sector in January this year was 40.4%, down 3.3 percentage points from December last year and contracting for seven consecutive months.
In the economic monitoring index system, PMI has 50% as its boundary line; an index greater than 50% indicates expansionary conditions, while an index below 50% indicates contraction.
In January, five components of Taiwan's PMI contracted in new orders, production, and employment, while supplier delivery times fell and inventories contracted.
All six major industries are reporting PMI contraction, with contraction speeds in descending order as follows: electrical and mechanical equipment industry (35.1%), electronic and optical industry (35.2%), chemical and biopharmaceutical healthcare industry (39.2%), basic materials industry (42.4%), transportation equipment industry (42.6%), and food and textile industry (45.7%).
Inflation-wise, Taiwan’s Main Counting and Statistical Office reported that the year-over-year increase of the Consumer Price Index (CPI) in January this year was 3.04%, which again surpassed the 3% mark since July last year.
Among them, vegetable prices jumped 28.25%, reaching their highest level in 17 months.
Taiwan’s Statistics Bureau specialist Cao Zhihong openly acknowledged that the price hikes for vegetables indeed exceeded expectations. Excluding the factors of the Spring Festival, the average CPI for January and February this year should be close to 2.71% from last December. Inflation pressure still exists and is at high levels.
Looking ahead to Taiwan’s economy this year, experts express pessimism based on reports from local media such as The United Daily News and Yahoo Finance.
Professor Wu Daren from the Economics Department of “Central University” in Taiwan analyzed that the export downturn could cause cash flow problems for export-manufacturing firms, leading to an increased risk of default on debts.
At the same time, reduced orders lead to firms cutting labor costs, which affects the labor market and household economies, thereby impacting consumption capacity.
Mr. Chou Ta-sing of the Institute of Taiwan Economic Research believes that the inflation situation in Europe and America is not resolved this year, and demand continues to shrink. Consequently, he forecasts that Taiwanese export will continue to suffer from decline throughout the first half of the year.
Due to Taiwan’s economy being supported by exports, its growth for the year is expected to be weaker than last year due to sluggish export performance.
Newly-appointed central committee members, alternate members, and main-level officials at provincial and ministerial levels complete the learning seminar on implementing Xi Jinping Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era and the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China - Rolling News - Hunan Daily - Huasheng Online
The newly elected members of the Politburo Standing Committee and alternate members of the Central Committee as well as leading cadres at provincial and ministerial levels have completed their training on learning and implementing Xi Jinping Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era and the spirit of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China.
2023-02-11 13:07:20 [Source: Xinhua News Agency] [Editor: Li Sufeng] Size: 【Large Medium Small】
Xinhua News Agency, Beijing, February 10 – The seminar for new members of the Central Committee, alternate members, and principal leading cadres at or above the ministerial level to study and implement Xi Jinping’s Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era and the spirit of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China concluded late yesterday afternoon at the Central Party School (National Academy of Governance). Central Political Bureau member and Secretary of the Central Secretariat Cai Qi attended the closing ceremony and delivered a summary speech.
He said that he would thoroughly study and implement the important speech delivered by General Secretary Xi Jinping at the opening ceremony of the seminar training class, with greater determination to uphold the “two establishments” and resolutely achieve the “two upholds,” strengthen his abilities and work hard to advance all tasks related to China’s modernization in accordance with the requirements of socialism with Chinese characteristics for a new era, and create achievements worthy of historical, practical, and people's judgment in fully building a modern socialist country and realizing the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation.
During the seminar, all participants guided by Xi Jinping's Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era, studied in depth the spirit of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China and President Xi Jinping's opening remarks at the seminar's start. They engaged in in-depth discussions and exchanges based on actual circumstances, deepening their understanding of a series of major theoretical and practical issues concerning China's modernization. This strengthened their confidence and determination to advance the great rejuvenation of the Chinese nation under the strong leadership of the Central Committee with Comrade Xi Jinping at its core. It also heightened their sense of responsibility and mission to perform their duties, do their work well, and ensure a good start to the new era and new journey.
At the graduation ceremony, 10 representatives from the seminar spoke, reporting on their learning gains and exchanging experiences.
Zai Cai Qi’s statement, studying and implementing Xi Jinping’s Thought on Socialism with Chinese Characteristics for a New Era and the spirit of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China is both a primary political task in the current and future period, and a long-term strategic task. It should be carried out according to the requirement of “comprehensively learning, comprehensively grasping, and fully implementing.” This will push the work of studying and implementing these ideas to go deeper, more practically, and more deeply into people’s hearts.
To more deeply understand the decisive significance of “two establishments,” to uphold Comrade Xi Jinping’s core position and the authority of the Central Committee of the Party and its centralized and unified leadership resolutely, and to continuously improve one’s political judgment, political insight, and political execution capabilities, always maintaining high consistency in terms of ideology, politics, and action with the Central Committee of the Party with Comrade Xi Jinping at its core.
To diligently master and apply Marxist theory as one’s forte, consciously arm oneself with the Party’s innovative theories to guide one’s thoughts, practice, and work, and strive to achieve deep study, meticulous understanding, and firm implementation in these areas; truly learn to acquire unwavering belief, absolute loyalty, and mission commitment.
To earnestly implement all decisions and deployments of the 20th National Congress of the Communist Party of China with an enterprising spirit, advance the Chinese-style modernization, roll up our sleeves to work hard, get down to business as a good “construction supervisor”, step by step turn the blueprint into reality.
It is imperative to remember that comprehensive and strict governance of the Party must be pursued at all times, and self-revolution within the Party must also continue forever. The political responsibility for comprehensive and strict governance of the Party should be pressed firmly, with party political construction serving as the overarching principle, and efforts should be made to advance the new great project of Party building in the new era.
To enhance our ability to promote high-quality development, serve the people, and manage and prevent risks, we must foster a strong tradition of investigation and research. We must resolutely prevent and overcome formalism and bureaucratism.
Shi Tiefeng, Li Ganjie, Li Shuei, Chen Wenqing, Liu JinGuo and Wang Xiaohong attended the graduation ceremony, and Chen Xi presided over it.
VNA Hanoi – VNA dispatch reporter has reported that Vietnam’s Prime Minister Nguyen Xuan Phuc and his wife have had an official visit to Singapore and Brunei successfully and obtained comprehensive, practical, and specific results.
Over the course of three days during his visit to Singapore and Brunei, Premier Van Minhang participated in more than 30 different activities.
The achievements injected new momentum for deepening, broadening, and enhancing both the strategic partnership between Vietnam and New Zealand and the comprehensive partnership between the two countries.
During his visit to both countries, Premier Pham Minh Chinh continued to reaffirm Vietnam’s and the country’s Party’s foreign policy orientation, which is characterized by independent and sovereign stance, diversification, dynamism, readiness to be good friends and reliable partners for all countries, and a responsible member of the international community.
Strengthening relations with Singapore and Brunei is each country’s need, aimed at enhancing the well-being of its people, and committed to peace, stability, and development in the region and the world.
At each meeting and negotiation session, Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh has agreed with leaders of Singapore and Brunei to strengthen political trust with Vietnam through high-level visits, effective implementation of bilateral cooperation mechanisms and important agreements in various ways.
Many cooperation documents were signed during this visit.
Among these, two major highlights include the Memorandum of Understanding on Green and Digital Economy Partnership signed with Singapore and the Action Plan for Strengthening Comprehensive Partnership between Vietnam and Brunei Darussalam for the 2023-2027 Period.
Vietnam signs Memorandum of Understanding on Partnership in Green and Digital Economy with Singapore.
Image from Vietnam News Agency
During meetings with business leaders, seminars, or attending economic forums, Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh emphasized that Vietnam welcomes and creates favorable conditions for expanding investment scopes in areas such as digital transformation, green energy, high-tech, and innovation and creativity by Singapore and Brunei enterprises in Vietnam.
This visit not only helps to deepen cooperation between Vietnam and Singapore and Brunei in traditional areas such as politics, diplomacy, economy, security, defense, education and training, oil and gas, tourism, people-to-people exchanges, but also creates frameworks for cooperation in new potential areas such as digital economy, green economy, energy transition, innovation and creativity, smart cities, and sustainable development.
Brunei's Sultan Hassanal Bolkiah and Prime Minister Pham Minh Duty are preparing to enter the bilateral meeting.
Image from VNA
During his visits to both countries, Pham Minh Chinh’s Prime Minister has made time to visit and listen to the thoughts and aspirations of Vietnamese expatriates living there.
During their leaders’ meetings, Prime Minister Pham Minh Prime suggested that both governments pay more attention to ensuring fair treatment for the local Vietnamese community, provide them with opportunities to contribute to the local society, and create favorable conditions for fostering relations between the two countries.
All of these suggestions were agreed to and supported by both countries' leaders.
In particular, Vice President Fang Mingzheng also shared with the leaders of both countries his desire for an ASEAN Community that is united, peaceful, stable and prosperous; they agreed to maintain unity and cooperation with ASEAN member states while enhancing their role as a regional and international leader in the complex and ever-changing geopolitical environment.
With its important achievements, Prime Minister Pham Minh Chinh made an official visit to Singapore and Brunei to effectively implement the Party’s Third Congress’ priority of strengthening relations with ASEAN neighbors through effective implementation of the 12th Conclusion (12-KL/TW) of the Central Committee Political Bureau on Vietnamese Foreign Affairs in the new situation, as well as making positive contributions to mobilizing the strength of the entire nation.
